lated literature based on our findings, especially work published from 2010-2026. Divide the section into subsections.\r\n\r\nCitation balance for the Literature Review: use approximately a 50/50 mix of \\cite{} (前引, author-as-subject) and \\citep{} (后引, parenthetical). Roughly half the citations should appear as the grammatical subject of a sentence (\"\\cite{baker2003} document that...\"), and roughly half should appear in parentheses (\"...consistent with prior work \\citep{diether2002}\"). After drafting, count both forms and rebalance toward 50/50.\r\n\r\nCite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints must be annotated with supporting evidence. List references with DOI link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n假说构建  prompt\r\n\r\nFormulate the first hypothesis H1 for this study based on the baseline regression results. Use 500 English words to provide reasonable argument for the hypothesis H1. The argument should incorporate the mechanisms documented in this study but should not mention the findings explicitly. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end. 先说理，后提出假说。阐述完理由后，加上一句，The first hypothsis... \r\n\r\nFormulate two other hypotheses H2 and H3 for this study that can summarize all cross-sectional heterogeneity (but you must act as if you do not know the empircal findiings). Use 700 English words to provide reasonable arguments for the hypotheses. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end. 先说理，后提出假说。阐述完理由后，加上一句，The second hypothsis... or the final hypothesis.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n理论模型 Prompt\r\nPlease describe in detail the setup of a theoretical model to support my empirical findings. Include the model's assumptions, variable definitions, and functional forms. The model should provide a unified explanatory framework for the empirical results. Use LaTeX format for mathematical formulas and provide detailed explanations in English. The model setup should be comprehensive and lay the groundwork for subsequent theorems and proofs. Do not use bullet points. Instead, present the information in a flowing, academic style suitable for a theoretical paper section.\r\n\r\nBased on the theoretical model setup previously described, please propose 1-2 key theorems that articulate the main conclusions of the model. These theorems should correspond to and explain the empirical findings. Then, provide detailed mathematical proofs for these theorems. The proof process should be logically rigorous with clear steps. Use LaTeX format for all mathematical content, including theorems and proofs. Provide necessary explanations in English throughout.\r\n\r\nAfter presenting the theorems and proofs, discuss the implications and limitations of this theoretical model. Explain how the model provides a theoretical foundation for the empirical findings, and suggest potential directions for model extensions.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n数据与样本构建 prompt\r\n\r\nUpload the whole paper and Stata do file.\r\nUse 300 English words to write a paragraph. Describe the above relevant data source in detail.\r\n\r\nSample:\r\nUpload the whole paper and Stata do file.\r\nUse 200 English words to write a paragraph. Describe the sample construction procedure. Talk about the final sample size\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n变量构建 prompt\r\nUse 600 American English words to write the section \\section{Variable Construction}. This section covers ONLY the dependent variable(s) and the core independent variable. DO NOT describe control variables here — control variables belong to the Empirical Model section.\r\n\r\nUse \\subsection{} blocks whose titles reflect the actual indicator content drawn from the variable definition table (e.g., \\subsection{Measuring Corporate Innovation}, \\subsection{Investor Disagreement}, \\subsection{ESG Disclosure Quality}). DO NOT use generic placeholder titles like \"Dependent Variable\" or \"Independent Variable\" — read the variable definition table first, then name the subsections after what each measure actually captures.\r\n\r\nFor each variable, explain its economic meaning, describe how it is measured (formulas, sources, transformations), and cite the original paper that proposed the measure. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid fabricated literature / data / conclusions. List references with DOI link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEmpirical Model prompt\r\nProduce the econometric model in LaTeX format (use $X$ to express the vector of all control variables, use Greek letters for various fixed effects). Use 500 American English words to describe the empirical model.\r\n\r\nBeyond the equation itself, this section MUST also describe the CONTROL VARIABLES (controls live here, not in Variable Construction). After presenting the equation, devote a paragraph or two to: list each control included in $X$, briefly justify its inclusion, describe its measurement, and cite supporting prior literature. Reference the variable definition table for precise definitions.\r\n\r\nAlso describe the dependent variable, core independent variable, fixed effects, and the rationale for the model specification (including standard error clustering). Do not use bullet points. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid fabricated literature / data / conclusions. List references with DOI link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n描述图片 prompt\r\nPlease suggest 2 or 3 figures that can be shown in this paper as descriptive results.\r\n\r\nCould you show the Stata code for drawing these figures?\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n描述统计 prompt\r\nUse 350 English words to write a paragraph for the descriptive statistics. Choose the most important variables rather than listing all variables. When you are describing the summary statistics, you need to report mean or other statistics when you see fit. \r\n\r\nUse 50 English words to describe the correlation matrix.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nBaseline Regression prompt\r\nUse 650 English words to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEndogeneity prompt\r\n\r\nUse 800 English words to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nRobustness checks prompt\r\n全部稳健性一次性写完，字数根据实际情况增减\r\n\r\nUse 1000 English words to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCross-sectional heterogeneity prompt\r\n（每个异质性维度 500 词，总词数 = 500 × 维度数）\r\nUse 500 English words per heterogeneity dimension to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nMechanism prompt\r\n（每个机制 600 词，总词数 = 600 × 机制数）\r\nUse 600 English words per mechanism to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nAlternative explanation prompt\r\nUse 750 English words to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFurther Analysis Prompt\r\nUse 650 English words to write for the section XX. Cite relevant and important literature published from 2010-2026. All responses must be based on academic facts. Avoid generating fabricated literature / data / conclusions. All viewpoints and content must be annotated with supporting evidence. List the reference with DOL link in APA format at the end.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nConclusion prompt\r\nUse 350 English words to write for the section XX.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nCover Letter and Highlights\r\n需上传论文pdf\r\nSuppose you are a well-known finance professor. Please draft a cover letter of 380 English words for my manuscript. Do not use bullet points.\r\nTarget Journal: 填入期刊名称\r\nAttach signature as follows:\r\nKai Wu, PhD\r\nAssociate Professor of Finance\r\nCentral University of Finance and Economics\r\nP. R. China\r\n\r\nSuppose you are a well-known finance professor. Please write 4 highlights, each with less than 150 characters including spaces. Do not report the number of letters. "
